{#- Deliberately nothing else. The kernel library is target-agnostic and must
    render BYTE-IDENTICAL from every C target: RUMOCA_GALEC_KERNELS_VERSION
    hashes the base templates, so a target-specific banner here would be
    different bytes under the same constant — the silent-`#error`,
    multiple-definition-at-link failure the constant exists to prevent. The
    base defines no overridable block, so an override added here would be
    ignored rather than silently forking the bytes. Conformance claims live
    in this target's model artifacts, which are the manifested Production
    Code representation. -#}
